  "problem": "A coastal research station is monitoring the population of brine shrimp in a controlled seawater tank. The tank can sustain a maximum population of $500$ shrimp, but the population is still below this limit. Since researchers began tracking the growth, the population reached $452$ shrimp on day $3$ and $473$ shrimp on day $9.$ On what day will the population reach $490$ shrimp? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population of shrimp, $P(t),$ increases at a rate that obeys an inhibited growth model, where $t$ is the time, in days.*",
